include/canlin/ev_limits.h:24 says the process-wide bounds are "smaller than the sum of module bounds". That holds for the item bound (512 < 16 x 64 = 1024) but is false for the byte bound: 16 module slots x 256 KiB = 4 MiB is exactly CANLIN_EV_PROC_MAX_BYTES, not smaller. The comment has to say what is true - that the process-wide byte bound is the sum of the module byte bounds - or the spec relation must be decided. Found by the 2026-11-15 review of k134.

